  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures the Mountain Goats performing at the Theatre of the Living Arts in Philadelphia on November 28, 2009 [1]. The band was on their initial North American tour to support their latest record [1]. For this leg, the standard trio was joined by an additional electric guitarist named Perry Owen Wright [1]. The Mountain Goats were also touring with Final Fantasy [1]. The setlist features twenty songs, including rare tracks like Handball and Song for Dana Plato [1]. Notable bustouts include One Fine Day, Going to Michigan, and Going to Bristol [1]. The performance also includes the first archived appearance of Hebrews 11:40 [1]. The recording is a 78-minute audio file taped and transferred by Thomas J Hartnett [1]. It is the only available recording of this specific show [1]. A listener review of this recording notes the high energy of the opening song [2]. The band provided spoken introductions for several tracks, including Cotton and Deuteronomy 2:10 [1]. This is the 147th show in the archive’s collection for the band [3]. The previous archived performance was held at the 9:30 Club on November 27, 2009 [3]. The encore consists of three songs, ending with The Best Ever Death Metal Band in Denton [1]. The recording offers a complete view of this tour stop [1].",
